# E. coli Biohydrogen Production: Metabolic Model Analysis

## Overview
This repository contains a computational analysis of hydrogen (H2) production in Escherichia coli using the genome-scale metabolic model iML1515.

The study focuses on metabolic pathways involved in hydrogen production and evaluates how different metabolic constraints and interventions affect hydrogen yield.

## Objectives
- Analyze the metabolic model of E. coli.
- Investigate the role of formate hydrogen lyase (FHL) in hydrogen production.
- Evaluate the influence of glucose uptake and growth rate on hydrogen yield.
- Assess the effects of selected metabolic pathway constraints.

## Tools and Methods
- Python
- Google Colab
- COBRApy
- Flux Balance Analysis (FBA)
- Genome-scale metabolic modeling

## Repository Contents
- `E_coli_biohydrogen_analysis.ipynb` – Jupyter notebook containing the computational analysis.
- `iML1515.xml.gz` – genome-scale metabolic model of E. coli.

## Note
All results presented in this repository are computational predictions obtained through metabolic modeling. They do not represent experimentally validated measurements.
